course: dictionary
lesson: 2536
title: Words for materials and things we wear
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A noun is a naming word. Deerskin is made from two smaller words, deer and skin, so it means the skin of a deer. When the skin is made soft, it becomes leather that people use for clothes, shoes and bags.
explain: Look at the clues in the story. «I had to pay two deerskins, soft ones with fringes, to the Stranger-man.» Two deerskins means two pieces of skin, and soft ones with fringes tells you what they were like. Tegumai is talking about paying for something, so deerskins must be valuable things that people could hand over.
explain: Some nouns name a material, like wood or gold, and you talk about them without counting. Deerskin works in the same way: you can say «soft deerskin» for the material. But when you mean single pieces, you can count them, as in «two deerskins». Ask yourself: am I talking about the stuff, or about pieces of it?
fact: Deerskin means the skin of a deer, especially when it is made into soft leather.
fact: Deerskin is used for clothes, moccasins, bags and soft gloves.
fact: Stone Age and Native American peoples used deerskin for clothes, moccasins and drums.
fact: In the Just So Stories, Taffy's mother and the other Neolithic ladies use deerskin.
fact: Deerskin is uncountable as a material, but you can say a deerskin or deerskins for single pieces.
exercise: «I had to pay two deerskins, soft ones with fringes.» What is a deerskin? | A type of Stone Age house | A loud musical instrument | *The skin of a deer, made soft for clothes or bags | A kind of cold drink
exercise: In history lessons, what did Stone Age people use deerskin for? | Glass windows | Plastic bottles | *Clothes and moccasins | Electric lights
exercise: «Daddy says he had to pay the Stranger-man two soft deerskins to say sorry.» Which word tells you the deerskins are single pieces you can count? | sorry | *two | Daddy | soft
test: Today deerskin leather is used for what? | Car engines | Roof tiles | *Soft gloves | Bicycle wheels
test: In the sentence «two deerskins», why is deerskins in the plural? | It is about a single cow | It is a verb | *It means more than one piece of deerskin | It is about a material, such as wood
exam: Which sentence uses deerskin for the material, not for counting pieces? | «Two deerskins were on the table.» | *«The gloves were made of soft deerskin.» | «Five deerskins hung on the wall.»
